  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Let The Good Times Roll** (1 review): Reviewer, who attended, found it a perfect way to open the night [3]\n- **Good Lovin** (1 review): Described as a rollicking version following Bertha [3]\n- **Cassidy** (1 review): The first-set Cassidy transported the crowd somewhere else entirely, according to the attendee [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Spanish Jam**: rare: 8 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Let The Good Times Roll [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2021-08-20.CitiFieldQueensNYC** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 199 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **deadco2021-08-20.CitiFieldFlushingNYNak700s**: audience recording; 20 songs; 202 min [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2021-08-20.CitiFieldQueensNYC**: taped by W Zimmerman; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Sennheiser Me-80 Mini Shotguns> GakCables > Mix Pre 6 @ 16/48 [1]. Also: Edited and tracked in Sound Forge Pro 13 from a 16/44.1 SD master, then converted to FLAC with Traders Little Helper [1]\n- **deadco2021-08-20.CitiFieldFlushingNYNak700s**: taped by JT/NY; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Nakamichi CM700's w 701 Caps > GakCables > Lunatec V3 > GakCables > Sound Devices 722 @ 24/96 [2]. Also: Lineage runs from a 16/44.1 SD master through Sound Forge Pro 13 tracking and editing, then FLAC conversion via Traders Little Helper [2]",
